        "text": "The upside risk is a broad hiring rebound, including stronger health care and hospitality gains, which could put the first print above 165 thousand and outside the interval. The downside risk is an abrupt private-sector contraction combined with government job losses, or a large strike or weather disruption affecting payroll counts, which could put it below -51 thousand and outside the interval."
